      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between 1910 and 1940, NDG’s housing boom produced a blend of Art Nouveau, Art Deco, and Beaux‑Arts styles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame-de-Gr%C3%A2ce",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first tramway in NDG appeared in 1908, running from Snowdon Station to Mount Royal and Parc avenues.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame-de-Gr%C3%A2ce",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Founded in 2022, the NDG Historical Society is gearing up to celebrate the neighborhood’s 150th anniversary in 2026.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
